WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.960
Help all kids learn and grow with PBS Kids.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.240
Thank you for supporting your PBS station.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.540
Crat Crat Brothers! I'm Martin.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.460
And I'm Chris.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.160
And these are rhinos.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:21.450
Famous for that prehistoric look, the tough armor-like skin, and that amazing horn.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.590
That horn and the weight behind it.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.550
If you had that charge in at you, not many creatures want to mess with a rhino.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.890
The third largest land animal in the world.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.820
Oh, and check out that horn.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.780
It's made of a special substance called keratin.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.040
The same stuff our fingernails are made of.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:37.640
And our hair.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.970
But in a rhino, it's woven together

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.380
to make a very light horn.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.540
But when the rhino smooths it out on the rocks,

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.120
it looks like, and is, a pretty awesome weapon.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.610
Rhinos are near-sighted.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.730
That means they can see things pretty well close up.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.490
But anything far away is a little blurry.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.840
And if they don't know what something is, they get nervous.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:05.920
that is when they charge. Rhinos have a special relationship with a bird that

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.480
gives a warning call whenever danger is near. The bird is called an oxpecker and

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.750
it hangs out on top of the rhino. The oxpecker picks ticks and parasites out

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.830
of the rhino's ears and off its skin, getting a meal and cleaning up the rhino.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.780
Everyone gets something out of the relationship and that kind of

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.350
relationship is called a symbiotic relationship. Creature teamwork, the

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:29.970
Rhino's horn.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.500
It's impressive size and it's charging power make the rhino one of the most impressive animals on earth

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.340
Imagine if we had the creature powers of the Rhino

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:41.820
What if?

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:18.890
Get rid of your powers and climb up and fly

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.520
Let the rhinos roll!

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.820
I am so stoked we found those missing rhinos.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.140
Yeah, me too! But the Criteria took a beating!

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.710
You can't jump a 20-foot ravine when we're still in truck mode, bro!

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.420
Hey, a charging hippo doesn't change modes, dude.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.820
I was going...

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:00.940
Hippopotamus!

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:01.700
Hmm.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.340
Just pass me the oil cap.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.880
I don't think an equatorial land snail's gonna work.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.250
Whoa!

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:24.220
What's going on with that black rhino?

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.330
I don't know.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.740
But we've gotta find out.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:35.390
Aviva, come in. Something strange happened to a black rhino in the Serengeti.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.690
I'll teleport you something that will give you a bird's eye view of the situation.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.440
Voila! Collapsible hang glider.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.340
Too slow! I got it! Show off.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.000
Woohoo! Let's go, bro!

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.280
We've got a creature mystery to solve.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:56.810
More rhinos. Maybe we'll find clues.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.840
Back up, Martin. Black rhinos are the most ready-to-charge rhinos in the world.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:18.070
Relax. If we don't move, she can hardly see us. Poor eyesight, remember?

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:27.700
But the nose and ears are super sensitive. That rhino will charge if we sound or even smell like a threat.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:29.970
I took a shower. Did you?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.290
How about cleaning those ears?

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:33.970
Oh!

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:38.290
I mean the oxpeckers, crawling right into the rhino's ears,

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.430
picking ticks like flying Q-tips.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.190
The rhinos get their ears cleaned, the birds get a meal.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.080
Both get something out of the deal.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.380
It's an amazing symbiotic relationship.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:50.840
Oh, yeah?

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:54.420
I think the coolest part is that the rhino can chill out and eat,

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.000
because the oxpecker will sound the danger alarm.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.060
Dude, you got me on that one.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:05.230
Uh, did we just set off the rhino alarm?

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.450
Yup, we set it off.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:09.460
Whoa!

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.090
Did you see that?

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.370
See it?

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.270
I felt it.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:22.790
Ouch.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.400
No, I mean the oxpeckers hung on even when the rhino charges.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.640
Now that's the coolest thing.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:38.850
Okay, you got me, but what I don't get is who would want to mess with the third heaviest land mammal on the planet and take on that charge?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.940
That's who the rhino was going for. We were just in the way. They're after the calf.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.620
That's a 3,000-pound Mega Mammal with some fancy footwork.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:14.160
Heard of Toss salad, but... Toss the lions?

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:15.600
Incoming!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:21.120
Ooh, that horn is a serious weapon.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.740
Rhino defense is awesome!

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:23.660
Huh? Huh?

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:32.560
Oh, no. I just tuned it up.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.920
I like it. Gives her character.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.460
You know, that made no sense.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:41.390
Black rhinos are solitary. They never stampede in a huge herd.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:42.460
It's unnatural.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:52.610
Are you okay?

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.980
That little nub of a horn you got.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:58.310
I'm gonna call you nubs.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:06:59.980
Oh, but there's...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.600
There's no way your mom would leave you behind, little buddy.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:06.890
Or not come charging towards a lost call.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:08.910
Something's very wrong here.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:09.950
Poachers?

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.600
I don't know, but we're going to find out.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:13.500
Let's track them.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.420
Uh-oh, don't look now, Chris.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.140
But someone's tracking us.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:23.990
They know there's no mom to protect them.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.460
We've got to get nubs out of here fast.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.040
I think I'll stick around.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.980
Something about that rhino stampede...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.040
It just didn't seem right.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:32.240
I got you, Nubs!

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:32.840
Whoa!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.200
Kreatera, don't fail us now.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:42.380
Later, lions!

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:47.230
What are you doing up there?

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.830
Getting a bird's eye view.

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.530
I'll take Nubs to safety and be right back.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:55.270
Don't get distracted and forget about me.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.480
Oh, don't worry.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:57.620
I won't leave you hanging.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.900
He always finds a way to hang out with a baby animal.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:09.430
A flock of oxpecker birds means a herd of some kind of creature is nearby.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.610
Rhinos! What is going on?

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:14.820
Gotta check this out!

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.470
Chris here! I'm definitely onto something!

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.690
I'll keep it posted! Over and out!

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.560
Take it off on my watch.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:54.840
Guys, I've got Nubs, a baby rhino.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.790
Nubs is a perfect name.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:08:59.970
I thought you...

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.170
I saved him from a bunch of lions.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.990
Teeth, claws, the works.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.120
Let's go with the disappearing rhinos.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.680
Oh, you know, Chris, he's all over it.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.580
With this little pumpkin in the HQ,

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:14.380
I can add some incredible rhino-inspired features

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.840
into the creature power suits.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.250
There you go, sweetie.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.470
I'm just gonna scan your skeleton.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.570
Keep him distracted, MK.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:28.690
Say, scare him.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.540
James, what kind of wild-eyed ranger is that?

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:57.090
Want to hear me snort like a rhino?

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.300
Should've known.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.700
It's another Zack attack on creatures.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.280
Knock it off, Martin.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:06.520
Zack can see you.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:07.780
He's spying on us.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:10.260
Green guy, glad you could stop by.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.320
And guess what?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.320
Your silly little creature pod doesn't work anymore,

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.620
so the blue boy can't hear you.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.240
Oh, too bad.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.100
Oh, hi.

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.470
Okay, I've got Nubsy all decoded.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.290
As soon as I have the program done,

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.910
you and Chris can try out your rhino-inspired suits.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:39.590
Chris, what am I doing?

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.080
I've been here forever.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.400
I've got to get back to Chris.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.040
Dude, it's me.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:44.960
I'm on my way.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.470
Stay where you are, bro.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:48.870
It was just a park ranger vaccinating rhinos.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:50.570
He already took care of the rhino calf.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:51.990
Keep it as long as you want

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.790
and have Aviva work on the disc for the creature power suit.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:55.670
Toodles!

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:57.740
Huh?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.160
Toodles?

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.430
Chris can be such a geek.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.140
But something about him didn't seem right.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.480
MK, I've got it. Get over here.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:12.690
Everyone has a bulldozer, but I have a rhino-dozer.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:15.490
Now with Blue Boy distracted,

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.430
I can finish building my rhino-dozers.

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:19.790
Rhino-dozers?

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:21.650
My greatest invention ever.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:24.350
With 3,000 pounds of strength,

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:27.790
I can dig up trees and flatten things

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.970
so I can build a parking lot.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.460
Leave the rhinos alone, Zack. They're seriously endangered.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:37.120
They belong living free and in the wild.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.940
Not this week. And you wild rats are gonna help me.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:47.410
And because I know Aviva, I knew the little rhino would inspire her to work on the creature power suit

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:51.750
and then reveal the charge code that I need for my rhino dozers.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:59.010
I gave the little rhino a contact lens with a camera feature so I can see everything going on in your headquarters.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:19.700
the charge code. Ready for testing. Yes. Told ya. No. Let's try a rhino horn. Working. Heavy.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:29.880
Oh, that's not what I want to watch. Stop acting goofy, blue boy. That's my bro.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.850
Sorry, MK. Hold still while I recalibrate the horn density.

00:12:36.390 --> 00:12:37.900
Like I have a choice.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:42.670
Alright, here's the DNA code that controls horn growth and their strong charge impulse.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:49.760
Posh! Capture. That's it. Now I have what I need for the rhino charge impulse.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:56.480
I chose the black rhino for their lack of brains. They'll charge at anything, even trees.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.800
Lay off, Zack. It's because they have poor eyesight.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.820
Dumbness.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.200
Poor eyesight.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:03.180
Whatever.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:07.040
But now that Aviva has delivered the rhino charge code,

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.820
I can control my rhino dozers!

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:11.300
Yeah!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.800
Relax, green guy.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.580
The only thing that can break through those bars is, uh,

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.130
well, nothing.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:24.360
But, prepare the rhino dozers to flatten the African savanna.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.510
I'll be back to deal with you later.

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:33.100
is feeling a little toasty.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:35.460
You're right.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.540
How do you keep an overheated rhino cool?

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:38.940
I know!

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.240
Oh, rhinos love mud.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:45.620
For four reasons, Aviva.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:47.020
It cools them down,

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.390
protects them from getting sunburned,

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:50.700
and keeps flies away.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.000
That's three.

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:53.670
And...

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.840
It feels great!

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.850
You just can't keep a rhino out of the mud.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.620
Looks like you can't keep a Martin out of it either.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.190
Hey, green guy.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.510
Still think I won't get away with it?

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:26.020
My rhino dozers will flood in anything I want them to.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.960
No way, Zack. I might be locked up, but...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:30.980
Martin will stop you.

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.120
Me, you pesky woodpeckers!

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:37.430
Try oxpeckers.

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:39.830
And they can't help being attracted to parasites.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.940
Think I'm funny, do you?

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.630
Me too, but you won't be laughing

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:48.330
when I knock down the barn hiding your turtle ship.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:49.950
You'll never find it.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.420
I already did.

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:55.430
The Rhino's contact lens also has a GPS feature

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:57.330
to find your exact location.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.170
Zach got your tongue?

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:06.860
Oh goody, we've arrived at the demolition location.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.380
Time to destroy some nature.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:12.780
Zachbots, prepare the rhino dozers.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:15.430
Let's get this parking lot started.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:37.200
That's it. Oxpeckers are the key to my escape.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:56.080
First tick. Let's see if this plan works.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.040
Hey, oxpecker, hungry?

00:15:58.440 --> 00:15:59.980
I've got a nice tasty tick for you.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:06.750
Not over. Do it for the rhino.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:12.640
Way to go, Oxbecker!

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.220
I'll pay you back by freeing the rhinos.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:22.940
Stand in the way of my rhino dozers!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.960
All right, Nubsy. If you ever get bored of...

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.640
Here's a totally awesome little creature for you to play with.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:37.870
Now we've got two orphans in our rescue center.

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:41.700
Oh, it's so great having nubs here.

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.590
But I guess I really should get him back to his mom.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:50.830
Yes, a contact lens?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.180
Since when do you wear contact lenses?

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:54.840
I don't.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.220
Time for a little demonstration.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.200
One flat barn coming up!

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:09.430
Why is it flashing red?

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.380
It's got Zach Barmitek written all over it.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.420
Oh, no, that's what was wrong.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.040
Chris was wearing red.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:20.610
He always wears green.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:23.110
And he'd never tell me to keep the rhino

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:24.230
for as long as I want.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:26.050
That couldn't have been him.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.160
Wait a sec.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:29.850
It also has a transmitter.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.690
With a tracking device!

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.230
Rhinos as bulldozers?

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.600
Yeah, and they're charging straight for us!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.100
Rhinos charge at 31 miles per hour,

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.000
and at 3,000 pounds per rhino?

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.180
That's a lot of force!

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.770
Enough to smash this hangar!

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.660
Oh, this is all my fault!

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.590
You were the bait all along!

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.300
And I led Zach right to us.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.020
It's not over yet.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.360
Koki, engage the emergency escape protocol.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:12.960
Oh no, hover power isn't engaging.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.180
Diverting all non-powered hover thrusters.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:22.110
Yes, gotta hover power.

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:50.200
Like you've never climbed before Chris you can make it

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:26.980
Zack's gonna run those rhinos into the ground we've got to stop him look I got us into this mess

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:29.980
I've got to get us out okay I'm pretty sure

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.600
sure there was a mud wallow around here.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.500
I remember seeing it too.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.620
It's past the baobab tree and then east to the water hole.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:39.650
First, I'm going to need help from this lion cub.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.530
Activate creature power suit.

00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:55.640
Now, I need you to help me pull this off, Nubs.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.430
Creature rescue!

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:03.960
Look what I got!

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:08.940
That's it.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:11.670
Protective Rhino Instinct Overriding Zack Control.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:12.650
Follow me!

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.680
So that's how you want to play!

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:31.170
I need your help now, Nubs.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.440
And not only will your mom respond to your call,

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:38.400
but other rhinos will.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:42.620
Right on, Nubs.

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:48.280
Stop me, wild rat.

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:49.710
So give up now.

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:59.960
Hurry, the rhino...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.260
Rhino's can't take much more! I gotta get Zach's remote!

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:04.840
Here's some Rhino power, Chris.

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:15.970
Like I always say, you can't keep a rhino out of the mud.

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:18.500
Let the rhinos run!

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:48.860
contaminated. Somebody save me. Later, Zach. Don't come by any time. Oh yeah, saving the planet with

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:57.270
creature power. Oh, it sure was great having a baby rhino to hang out with.

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:08.110
You'll always have the rhino power suit to remind you of nubs. He's with his mom where he belongs and all the rhinos are back

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:12.190
Living free and in the wild. Hey, what were you thinking bro?

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:19.580
I'd never tell you to keep a rhino calf back at the HQ. I know and since when do I wear red shirts?

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:27.150
Yeah, I may have been a little distracted a little and you thought I'd say toodles. I never say toodles

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:29.830
I did think that was pretty dorky

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:31.260
even for you.

00:23:41.410 --> 00:23:43.530
Symbiotic relationships are awesome.

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:45.800
Great examples of creature teamwork.

00:23:46.220 --> 00:23:48.780
And the Rhino and the Oxpecker make a great team.

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.140
They each get something out of the relationship.

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:54.900
The Rhino gets all the ticks and blood-sucking parasites

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:56.180
picked off its body.

00:23:56.640 --> 00:23:58.520
And the Oxpecker gets a tasty meal

00:23:58.520 --> 00:23:59.980
and a good place to purr.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:04.940
And from that place, the oxpecker also gives the rhino a warning system,

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:08.560
sounding the alarm if any danger or predators approach.

00:24:09.110 --> 00:24:13.900
There are all kinds of amazing symbiotic relationships all over the creature world.

00:24:15.990 --> 00:24:20.050
One other great example of symbiotic relationships is under the sea,

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:22.180
the clownfish and the anemone.

00:24:23.160 --> 00:24:27.040
The anemone is an amazing invertebrate with stinging tentacles,

00:24:27.140 --> 00:24:29.960
and the clownfish is the only fish that can...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.160
swim safely through the anemone without getting stung.

00:24:33.420 --> 00:24:35.520
So the anemone gives the clownfish protection,

00:24:35.760 --> 00:24:39.140
and the clownfish brings the anemone little bits of food.

00:24:39.380 --> 00:24:42.120
It's a classic symbiotic relationship.

00:24:45.130 --> 00:24:47.770
And maybe the most surprising symbiotic relationship

00:24:47.770 --> 00:24:52.310
we've ever seen was when we stumbled upon some warthogs

00:24:52.310 --> 00:24:55.150
that were hanging out with a group of banded mongoose.

00:24:55.330 --> 00:24:59.430
The warthog was approaching really close to the mongoose.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.500
We weren't sure what was going to happen.

00:25:01.990 --> 00:25:04.910
The warthog walked right up to the mongoose, and they didn't run.

00:25:05.700 --> 00:25:07.720
And then the warthog, he lay down.

00:25:09.090 --> 00:25:11.130
The mongoose approached and started climbing on it.

00:25:11.270 --> 00:25:14.750
They started nibbling his ear, picking ticks off the warthog's body.

00:25:15.600 --> 00:25:18.900
The mongoose were getting a meal, and the warthog was getting cleaned.

00:25:19.210 --> 00:25:22.850
Now that was a really cool and bizarre symbiotic relationship.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:29.620
These rhinos, the white rhinos, also live in croupes.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.340
but they don't always get along.

00:25:32.550 --> 00:25:33.920
Oh wow, cool.

00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:38.530
But for the most part, a group of 10 white rhinos,

00:25:38.570 --> 00:25:40.010
they graze pretty peacefully.

00:25:42.540 --> 00:25:44.960
We have a symbiotic relationship here going.

00:25:45.160 --> 00:25:46.620
We get to check out a cool creature

00:25:46.620 --> 00:25:48.200
and the rhino gets scratched.

00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:53.560
So that's the end of this episode.

00:25:53.820 --> 00:25:55.500
Keep on creature adventuring.

00:25:55.660 --> 00:25:56.940
We'll see you on the creature trail.

00:25:57.430 --> 00:25:58.290
See you later, bud.

00:26:17.470 --> 00:26:18.940
To find out more about cool animals,

00:26:19.860 --> 00:26:22.420
collect your own Wild Kratz creature powers,

00:26:22.720 --> 00:26:27.340
go to the Wild Kratz website, pskidsgo.org.

00:26:27.460 --> 00:26:28.440
We'll see you there!
